---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
---
<Figure width="full" stage title="Niches, deme by deme" sub="Each board is one deme's map of niches; a bar is the best program in its cell, taller when closer to the best known value.">
  <Fragment slot="controls">
    <button class="playb" id="nplay">Pause</button><span class="num" id="nIt" style="color:var(--ink);font-size:12.5px;min-width:110px"></span>
  </Fragment>
  <div class="nichegrid">
    <div id="niche3d" class="three"><canvas id="cniche"></canvas><div class="ov" id="ovniche"></div><div class="tip" id="tipniche" hidden></div></div>
    <div class="fig relwrap" id="vqmap"><p class="lab" style="margin:0 0 10px">The niches themselves</p></div>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>A newcomer only competes with its own niche.</b> <b>Boards:</b> across, the run's twelve learned niches (kinds
    of program, grouped automatically by their code); back to front, score bins. <b>Map:</b> the same twelve niches as
    points, placed by the two main directions of the code embedding; a bubble's size is how many demes hold their best
    program there. The grouping is refitted as the population moves, so a new kind of program opens a new niche
    instead of being thrown out. Hover a bar or a bubble for details.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
<figure class="figure wide">
  <p class="lab">The machinery around the population, in this run</p>
  <div class="mach" id="mach"></div>
</figure>
